{
  "dom_id": "step-q64102",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "The total area, in square meters,  covered by blueberry bushes in a forest can be modeled by the expression $800\\cdot (1.1)^{t},$ where $t$ is the number of years since the year $2015.$ What does the base of the exponential expression $(1.1)$ mean in this context?",
  "worked_solution": "The answer choices require interpretation as a percent, and so we use the growth rate formula.\n\nThe given expression is an exponential growth expression of the form $y(t)=a\\cdot (1+r)^{t}$, where:\n\n- $a=800$ represents the initial area covered by the  blueberry bushes\n\n- $1+r=1.1,$ where $r$ is the growth rate\n\n- $t$ is the number of years since $2015$\n\nSolving for $r$:\n\n$$\n1+r=1.1\\,⟹\\,r=0.1\n$$\n\nNow, $0.1$ (expressed as a percent) is equal to $10%.$ Therefore, the area covered by the bushes grows at a rate of $10%$ per year.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
